WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.158
Would you disagree when everyone raises a hand?

00:00:03.158 --> 00:00:06.316
Beyond the answer lies a need to belong.

00:00:06.316 --> 00:00:09.474
Asch studied line judgments in the 1950s.

00:00:09.474 --> 00:00:12.632
Simple judgments were placed in a group setting.

00:00:12.632 --> 00:00:15.789
A majority could influence an individual choice.

00:00:15.789 --> 00:00:22.105
Others can serve as sources of information.

00:00:22.105 --> 00:00:28.421
We may also worry about standing apart.

00:00:28.421 --> 00:00:34.737
Both influences can appear in one setting.

00:00:34.737 --> 00:00:41.053
This schematic does not collect experimental results.

00:00:41.053 --> 00:00:44.211
More votes do not change the line’s length.

00:00:44.211 --> 00:00:47.368
Disagreement does not automatically make one right.

00:00:47.368 --> 00:00:50.526
Task, culture, relationships and power matter.

00:00:50.526 --> 00:00:56.842
Write a judgment and reason before discussion.

00:00:56.842 --> 00:01:03.158
Compare evidence and allow dissent to explain.

00:01:03.158 --> 00:01:06.316
Safe expression needs practical arrangements.

00:01:06.316 --> 00:01:09.474
Listen to others and keep checking for yourself.

00:01:09.474 --> 00:01:12.632
A group can use its strength to include difference.

00:01:12.632 --> 00:01:15.789
Leave a seat for a different reason.
